    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d705">

                <pb facs="0602" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/610</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-22">April 22, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The British Ambassador<anchor n="14" xml:id="d705-f1"/> called to see me this
                    morning at his request.</p>
                <p>The Ambassador again raised the question of the recognition by the United States
                    of the independence of Syria. I replied that, in view <pb facs="0603" n="591"
                        xml:id="pg591"/> of the events in France in the past few days, I felt that
                    the time would soon come when this Government would wish to give further
                    consideration to this question. I took occasion to communicate to the Ambassador
                    the substance of Mr. Engert’s telegram of this morning<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d705-f2"/> indicating the complete discord between the Free French
                    representative in Syria and the British representative, General Spears. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d705-f1" n="14" xml:id="d705-f1-content">
                <p>Viscount Halifax.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d705-f2" n="15" xml:id="d705-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably telegram No. 142 of April 21, <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
